        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catlin%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first permanent settlement in Vermilion County began in Catlin in 1820, with James Butler as the first settler.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catlin%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1822, Catlin established the county’s first cemetery, God's Acre, marking early community organization.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catlin%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The first mill in both Vermilion and Champaign Counties, a corncracker, was built in Catlin in 1823 by James Butler.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catlin%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Catlin’s salt works, started in 1824, drew settlers with twenty-four kettles each holding 100 gallons, illustrating early industrial activity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catlin%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "In 1830, Grandma Guyman became Catlin’s first doctor and midwife, delivering over 1,000 babies to the growing township.",
